  "root": ".repo",
  "why": "B21 / D6. ASP.NET Core wires an implementation behind an interface with `services.AddScoped<IMailer, SmtpMailer>()`; every consumer is handed `IMailer`, so without an edge from `SmtpMailer` to `IMailer` a change to the implementation reaches none of its callers. `PROVIDES` (the edge Kotlin's Hilt bindings introduced) says exactly that: this declaration makes this type available for injection. `TryAdd*` registers the same way. A single-type `AddTransient<Worker>()` binds nothing behind an interface, so it has no edge. A factory whose lambda body is exactly one `new DbAudit()` builds `DbAudit`, so it is read (B22, D9).",
